## Summary
The Russian army advances towards Kharkiv, with Vovchansk as the next target. Ukrainian President Zelensky acknowledges the situation as extremely difficult. Russia accuses the West of supplying weapons used to strike Belgorod.

## Key Points
- Russian army advancing towards Kharkiv with Vovchansk as the next objective
- Ukrainian President Zelensky describes the situation as 'extremely difficult'
- Russia claims Western-supplied weapons were used in an attack on Belgorod


